{:edb/db-before-t 2810 :edb/db-after-t 2811 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536123 50 #inst "2026-10-09T15:43:16.683Z" 13194139536123 true] [17592186119757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384653 13194139536123 true] [17592186119757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384660 13194139536123 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384638 13194139536123 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384668 13194139536123 true] [17592186119759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384646 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384639 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384642 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384644 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1089 "q-326901" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1100 "Given the Cartesian equation $2x-y+2z+6=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$ \n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,$\n{{field-2}}\n, \n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1113 #uuid "925e27d5-9a24-540e-b569-c14fe85a8802" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384638 1145 "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨2,-1,2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+2z+6 & =0 \\\\ z & =-x+\\frac{y}{2}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-3)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-3⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-3⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,-1,2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384640 13194139536123 true] [17592186384639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384641 13194139536123 true] [17592186384639 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536123 true] [17592186384639 1041 "field-1" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384639 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384641 13194139536123 true] [17592186384639 1110 #uuid "404719b6-4d8f-5e11-9be9-036bda1402f6" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384640 1034 "3" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384640 1111 #uuid "2346d3ff-5938-5252-b9cd-952c41afb699" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384641 1034 "-3" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384641 1111 #uuid "89228a02-e815-56ab-9fbf-a197e79a148d" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384643 13194139536123 true] [17592186384642 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536123 true] [17592186384642 1041 "field-2" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384642 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384643 13194139536123 true] [17592186384642 1110 #uuid "565e5b01-c043-5165-b017-b140005d6c7b" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384643 1034 "-1" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384643 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384643 1111 #uuid "c388a551-0e74-54e5-9839-9cca156461dc" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384645 13194139536123 true] [17592186384644 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536123 true] [17592186384644 1041 "field-3" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384644 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384645 13194139536123 true] [17592186384644 1110 #uuid "206cc8c3-2056-520b-a460-0d49602ce8e2" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384645 1034 "2" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384645 1111 #uuid "523b3861-685d-571c-988d-ea0188229f52" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384646 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384647 13194139536123 true] [17592186384646 1089 "q-33142" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384646 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536123 true] [17592186384646 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(2,-5,1)$, $P(4,-2,3)$ and $Q(5,1,0).$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384646 1113 #uuid "c5938084-81eb-59aa-b8c4-275f8497be94" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384646 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨2,-5,1⟩,\\,p=⟨4,-2,3⟩,$ and $q=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,3⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,2⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨5,1,0⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-15i+8j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-15,8,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z+67 & =0 \\\\ 15x-8y-3z-67 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384648 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384649 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384650 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384651 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384652 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1041 "selection" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384648 13194139536123 true] [17592186384647 1110 #uuid "362de8bd-fdfa-5aa6-b00e-5111d888298e" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384648 1034 "15x-8y-3z-67=0" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384648 1111 #uuid "55723dcb-605f-595d-8fae-1ee5436e7a81" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384649 1034 "2x-5y+z-70=0" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384649 1111 #uuid "42a8ae72-16c3-587a-a3e7-b75bffe928ae" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384650 1034 "5x+y-67=0" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384650 1111 #uuid "803a1755-2134-5aa8-a86a-8015bacc22d9" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384651 1034 "15x-8y-3z+70=0" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384651 1111 #uuid "2bd5cb89-4f60-5887-afe3-a7c5a3523298" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384652 1034 "4x-2y+3z=0" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384652 1111 #uuid "31dcdae4-9b1f-53d5-a9d2-7fbe89fc944a" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384654 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384656 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384658 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1089 "q-336110" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=4+3t \\\\ y=1-4t \\\\ z=-3-2t\\end{aligned}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-4y\\,-\\,$ \n{{field-2}} $z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$\\,=0$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1113 #uuid "2c496c1b-87a2-58b0-9bd2-be54b651106d" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384653 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-2,5⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-4,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-4,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =⟨1,-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =1 \\\\ 3x-4y-2z & =1 \\\\ 3x-4y-2z-1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384655 13194139536123 true] [17592186384654 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536123 true] [17592186384654 1041 "field-1" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384654 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384655 13194139536123 true] [17592186384654 1110 #uuid "f08ab864-495e-565c-a51c-18ba0a886950" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384655 1034 "3" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384655 1111 #uuid "7fde512d-6ec1-5523-9f7e-f1e5a94c1668" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384657 13194139536123 true] [17592186384656 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536123 true] [17592186384656 1041 "field-2" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384656 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384657 13194139536123 true] [17592186384656 1110 #uuid "0d8b4801-7443-5015-9570-7463ee433851" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384657 1034 "2" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384657 1111 #uuid "ec6f1fa2-0c28-5b15-b0e2-c385a4c95fc9" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384659 13194139536123 true] [17592186384658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536123 true] [17592186384658 1041 "field-3" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384659 13194139536123 true] [17592186384658 1110 #uuid "fdd60602-2771-5921-8d18-9737745e767b" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384659 1034 "1" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536123 true] [17592186384659 1111 #uuid "85277b5a-1a68-5e4c-b1e5-9d1d322b6907" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384661 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384664 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384666 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1089 "q-336201" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,3,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$3x\\,-\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$y\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$=0$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1113 #uuid "db29741f-b982-55e1-b925-152441611363" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384660 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-2,3,1⟩.$  From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-5,2⟩.$  So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-5,2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =⟨-2,3,1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z & =-19 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z+19 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384661 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384662 13194139536123 true] [17592186384661 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384663 13194139536123 true] [17592186384661 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536123 true] [17592186384661 1041 "field-1" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384661 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384663 13194139536123 true] [17592186384661 1110 #uuid "ab8b83ee-829c-5df6-be8e-efc7065c5235" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384662 1034 "-5" 13194139536123 true] [17592186384662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13